<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Aug consumer prices up 0.1 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Aug consumer prices up 0.1 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo area consumer prices rose 0.1 percent in August from a year earlier but fell 0.1 percent month on month, the Management and Coordination Agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>Japan nationwide consumer prices for July increased 0.4 percent from a year earlier but dropped 0.1 percent from the previous month.</p>
<p>Month-on-month figures are not adjusted for seasonal factors.  </p>
<p>The breakdown of consumer prices in Tokyo and nationwide is as follows (index base 1995):</p>
<p>				   AUG	 JULY	  JUNE</p>
<p> Tokyo overall index	 99.9	100.0	 100.0</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	 +0.1 pct   +0.4 pct    -0.1 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes     -0.1 pct    0.0 pct    -0.4 pct</p>
<p> Tokyo core index	   99.7	 99.9	 100.1</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	  0.0 pct   +0.2 pct    +0.1 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes     -0.2 pct   -0.2 pct    -0.1 pct</p>
<p>				  July	 June	   May</p>
<p> Nationwide overall index 100.1	100.2	 100.5</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	  +0.4 pct    0.0 pct    +0.2 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	-0.1 pct   -0.3 pct    +0.2 pct</p>
<p> Nationwide core index    100.1	100.3	 100.3</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	  +0.3 pct   +0.2 pct    +0.1 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	-0.2 pct    0.0 pct    +0.1 pct</p>
<p>(NOTE: The Tokyo index was calculated by collecting price data at mid-month. The core index, which is a key barometer for gauging core inflation, is overall prices minus fresh food prices. The base year was changed to 1995 from 1990.)</p>
